---
// After CI: what version.cam adds to a recording, what it is planned to
// cost, and the sign-in button, which says the beta is private: you can't
// buy a plan yet, and the first ten people who ask get Pro free. Two ruled columns in the page's own grammar, no
// cards: on the left what it adds, on the right the plans as rows, each
// with its planned price in the machine's amber numerals and the word
// planned beside it, so a reader who never reaches the note still reads
// the price as a plan. The one picture is live: the badge of the recorder's
// own repository, so it is a receipt and not an illustration.
import { LinkButton } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

// Drawn by version.cam's own API, so no visitor's request leaves the site
// for a third party; a README may still let shields.io draw the same JSON.
const BADGE = 'https://api.version.cam/v1/badge/versioncam/versioncam/svg';
---

<div class="vc-hosted not-content">
	<section class="vc-hosted-col">
		<h3>What it adds</h3>
		<dl class="vc-hosted-what">
			<div>
				<dt>A permanent link that only plays versions that passed their check</dt>
				<dd>
					<code>clips.version.cam/&lt;owner&gt;/&lt;repo&gt;/&lt;clip&gt;</code> plays the newest
					version from your default branch that passed its check. When a clip breaks, the link keeps
					playing the last version that passed, and the dashboard shows that the clip is broken.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Embeds, GIFs and screenshots</dt>
				<dd>
					You get an embed for your own pages and oEmbed, so a link pasted into Notion or Slack shows
					the video. You also get a GIF for the README, and a screenshot of any frame or step when you
					ask for one.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>One link for a phone and a desktop</dt>
				<dd>
					Write a second clip at a phone's viewport and name it <code>&lt;clip&gt;-mobile</code>. The
					clip's page and its embed then play the phone video on a narrow screen and the desktop video
					on a wide one. You write two scripts because the app lays itself out differently on each;
					the shared name links them.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Clips on the pull request</dt>
				<dd>
					We add a check to the commit and post one comment on the pull request, which we update as
					you push to the branch. It shows a picture of each clip that looks different or failed.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>A badge that names the commit</dt>
				<dd>
					<a class="vc-badge" href="https://clips.version.cam/versioncam/versioncam"
						><img
							src={BADGE}
							alt="demo verified, the commit and how long ago, for the recorder's own repository"
							height="20"
						/></a
					>
					<span
						>The badge names the commit whose CI run published the recordings. The badge on this page is live: it
						shows the recorder's own repository.</span
					>
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Alerts when a clip breaks</dt>
				<dd>
					On Pro, when a clip breaks on your default branch, we email you, post to Slack or open a
					GitHub issue. We remind you two days later and then weekly, until the clip passes or someone
					acknowledges it.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Private repositories, on Pro</dt>
				<dd>
					Clips from a private repository play only for people who can read that repository on
					GitHub, through short-lived signed links. We store recordings in Cloudflare's EU
					jurisdiction.
				</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<section class="vc-hosted-col is-plans">
		<h3>Planned prices</h3>
		<dl class="vc-plans">
			<div>
				<dt>Free <span class="vc-num">$0</span></dt>
				<dd>
					For public repositories. Three projects, ten clips per project, thirty days of history,
					clips up to sixty seconds long, 1 GB of storage. Includes the pull request check and the
					badge.
				</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Pro <span class="vc-num">$35</span> per project, per month <span class="vc-planned">planned</span></dt>
				<dd>
					Adds private repositories. Their clips play only for people who can read the repository on
					GitHub. Unlimited history and
					a hundred clips per project. We email you, post to Slack or open a GitHub issue when a clip
					breaks. $350 a year.
				</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
		<p class="vc-plans-note">
			Priced per project, not per seat. The prices are marked "planned" because we will confirm them
			after the first invoices. Accounts from the beta pay 20% less for their first twelve months.
			Prices for ten or more projects are in <a href="/more/version-cam/">the docs</a>. The recorder
			and the Action stay free, with or without a plan.
		</p>
		<div class="vc-door">
			<LinkButton href="https://app.version.cam/" icon="right-arrow">Sign in with GitHub</LinkButton>
			<p>
				<strong>Private beta.</strong> You can't buy a plan yet, and we don't ask for a card. Free
				works for public repositories as soon as you sign in. The first ten people who ask get Pro
				free on their account until the beta ends. To ask, sign in, then email{' '}
				<a href="mailto:hello@version.cam">hello@version.cam</a> with your account name. The details are on the <a
					href="/more/version-cam/">How version.cam works</a
				> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>
